{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/architecture/desktop-themes.md; git diff f1e58da -- crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs crates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs apps/desktop/src/shell/feature-view.tsx apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts apps/desktop/src/app.tsx'","aggregated_output":"# Desktop color themes\n\nThe desktop owns two independent preferences: appearance (`system`, `light`,\n`dark`) and color theme (`prismaAirs`, `gruvbox`). Prisma AIRS is the default.\nNeither preference updates an Academy account or unlocks an earned cosmetic.\n\nExisting state without `colorTheme` defaults to Prisma AIRS and retains its\nappearance. The default is omitted when saving; an alternate theme is saved as\nan explicit field. Invalid theme values remain a storage error, rather than\nsilently overwriting the preference. Existing atomic storage writes apply.\n\nOlder binaries use strict field validation and can reject state written with a\nnew preference. Opening an upgraded data directory with an older release is\nunsupported; this change does not claim downgrade compatibility or silently\nreset data. Preserve the state before any explicitly requested downgrade.\n\nThe document's general Academy theme continues to follow appearance. Desktop\npalette tokens are independent, and shared presentation colors are adapted only\ninside desktop theme scopes. Academy content and its portals keep the general\nAcademy palette. Earned Academy themes remain under Academy's existing rules.\ndiff --git a/apps/desktop/src/app.tsx b/apps/desktop/src/app.tsx\nindex 9aabf0d2..58236e3c 100644\n--- a/apps/desktop/src/app.tsx\n+++ b/apps/desktop/src/app.tsx\n@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@ export function App({ client }: { client: DesktopClient }) {\n                     // The shell's scope follows the snapshot before it renders: a\n                     // notification for another tenant or context is never surfaced.\n                     useShellStore.getState().setScope(next.active?.tenant ?? null, next.active?.context ?? null, next.switchBlocked?.review ?? null)\n+                    useShellStore.getState().observeWorkbench(next.active?.tenant ?? null, next.active?.context ?? null, next.workbench.collection?.scope ?? null)\n                     setSnapshot(next)\n                 },\n                 onMenu: (command) => onMenu.current(command),\n@@ -134,9 +135,10 @@ export function App({ client }: { client: DesktopClient }) {\n     }, [storage, resetFailed])\n \n     const appearance = snapshot?.appearance\n+    const colorTheme = snapshot?.colorTheme\n     // Apply the theme in the same commit as the snapshot, before paint, so\n     // the shell never shows a frame in the previous theme.\n-    useLayoutEffect(() => (appearance ? followAppearance(appearance) : undefined), [appearance])\n+    useLayoutEffect(() => (appearance ? followAppearance(appearance, colorTheme) : undefined), [appearance, colorTheme])\n \n     if (failure && !snapshot) {\n         return (\ndiff --git a/apps/desktop/src/shell/feature-view.tsx b/apps/desktop/src/shell/feature-view.tsx\nindex 232e603d..2e1b38bc 100644\n--- a/apps/desktop/src/shell/feature-view.tsx\n+++ b/apps/desktop/src/shell/feature-view.tsx\n@@ -1,12 +1,14 @@\n import { forwardRef, useId, useState } from 'react'\n-import { Button, Callout } from '@ai-security-academy/presentation'\n+import { Callout } from '@ai-security-academy/presentation'\n import { Info } from 'lucide-react'\n-import type { FeatureEntry, Intent, ShellSnapshot, Theme } from '@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts'\n+import type { FeatureEntry, ShellSnapshot, Theme } from '@prisma-airs/desktop-contracts'\n import { type Dispatch, outcomeMessage } from '../modules/tenants/dispatch'\n import { DiagnosticsPanel } from '../modules/diagnostics/diagnostics-panel'\n import { AcademyAccount } from '../modules/academy/academy-account'\n import { TenantsSettings } from '../modules/tenants/tenants-settings'\n import type { ObserveManagement } from '../modules/administration/management-read'\n+import { PageIntro } from '../v2/page-intro'\n+import { SetupWarningHistory } from '../v2/setup-warning-history'\n \n interface HeadingProps {\n     id: string\n@@ -25,11 +27,10 @@ export const PageHeading = forwardRef<HTMLHeadingElement, HeadingProps>(function\n     )\n })\n \n-export const UnavailableView = forwardRef<HTMLHeadingElement, { feature: FeatureEntry }>(function UnavailableView({ feature }, ref) {\n+export const UnavailableView = forwardRef<HTMLHeadingElement, { feature: FeatureEntry }>(function UnavailableView({ feature }) {\n     const planned = feature.availability.state === 'unavailable' ? feature.availability.plannedChunk : ''\n     return (\n-        <section aria-labelledby={`${feature.id}-heading`} data-slot='feature-unavailable'>\n-            <PageHeading ref={ref} id={`${feature.id}-heading`} kicker='Not available' title={feature.label} />\n+        <section aria-label={feature.label} data-slot='feature-unavailable'>\n             <Callout tone='default' icon={Info}>\n                 <p>\n                     {feature.label} is not available in this build. Nothing here contacts a Prisma AIRS\n@@ -43,12 +44,6 @@ export const UnavailableView = forwardRef<HTMLHeadingElement, { feature: Feature\n     )\n })\n \n-const THEMES: { value: Theme; label: string; hint: string }[] = [\n-    { value: 'system', label: 'Match System', hint: 'Follow the macOS appearance' },\n-    { value: 'light', label: 'Light', hint: 'Paper light theme' },\n-    { value: 'dark', label: 'Dark', hint: 'Gruvbox dark theme' },\n-]\n-\n interface SettingsProps {\n     snapshot: ShellSnapshot\n     pending: boolean\n@@ -58,47 +53,50 @@ interface SettingsProps {\n }\n \n export const SettingsView = forwardRef<HTMLHeadingElement, SettingsProps>(function SettingsView(\n-    { snapshot, pending, onSetAppearance, dispatch, observeManagement },\n-    ref\n+    { snapshot, pending, onSetAppearance, dispatch, observeManagement }\n ) {\n     const legend = useId()\n-    const appearance = snapshot.appearance\n+    const [themeBusy, setThemeBusy] = useState(false)\n+    const [message, setMessage] = useState<string | null>(null)\n+    async function setColorTheme(theme: ShellSnapshot['colorTheme']) {\n+        setThemeBusy(true)\n+        setMessage(null)\n+        const outcome = await dispatch({ kind: 'setColorTheme', theme })\n+        setThemeBusy(false)\n+        setMessage(outcomeMessage(outcome))\n+    }\n     return (\n-        <section aria-labelledby='settings-heading' data-slot='settings'>\n-            <PageHeading ref={ref} id='settings-heading' kicker='Desktop' title='Settings' />\n-            <fieldset aria-labelledby={legend} aria-busy={pending} className='border-academy-rule flex flex-col gap-3 rounded-[12px] border p-5'>\n-                <legend id={legend} className='text-academy-ink px-1 text-[15px] font-semibold'>\n-                    Appearance\n-                </legend>\n-                <p className='text-academy-ink-soft text-[13px]'>\n-                    A desktop-wide preference. It does not change your Academy account settings.\n-                </p>\n-                {THEMES.map((option) => (\n-                    <label key={option.value} className='flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center gap-3'>\n-                        <input\n-                            type='radio'\n-                            name='appearance'\n-                            value={option.value}\n-                            checked={appearance === option.value}\n-                            onChange={() => onSetAppearance(option.value)}\n-                            className='accent-[var(--academy-accent)] size-4'\n-                        />\n-                        <span className='flex flex-col'>\n-                            <span className='text-academy-ink text-[14px] font-medium'>{option.label}</span>\n-                            <span className='text-academy-ink-faint text-[12px]'>{option.hint}</span>\n-                        </span>\n-                    </label>\n-                ))}\n-            </fieldset>\n-            <div className='mt-6'>\n+        <section aria-label='Settings' data-slot='settings' className='flex flex-col gap-4'>\n+            <PageIntro description='Personalize the desktop, manage tenant connections and review local diagnostics.' />\n+            <div className='settings-grid'>\n+                <fieldset aria-labelledby={legend} aria-busy={pending || themeBusy} className='settings-card'>\n+                    <legend id={legend}>Appearance</legend>\n+                    <p className='settings-description'>Desktop preferences do not change your Academy account settings.</p>\n+                    <div className='settings-fields'>\n+                        <label className='settings-field'>\n+                            Appearance\n+                            <select aria-label='Appearance' value={snapshot.appearance} disabled={pending} onChange={(e) => onSetAppearance(e.target.value as Theme)}>\n+                                <option value='system'>Match system</option>\n+                                <option value='light'>Light</option>\n+                                <option value='dark'>Dark</option>\n+                            </select>\n+                        </label>\n+                        <label className='settings-field'>\n+                            Theme\n+                            <select aria-label='Theme' value={snapshot.colorTheme} disabled={themeBusy} onChange={(e) => void setColorTheme(e.target.value as ShellSnapshot['colorTheme'])}>\n+                                <option value='prismaAirs'>Prisma AIRS</option>\n+                                <option value='gruvbox'>Gruvbox</option>\n+                            </select>\n+                        </label>\n+                    </div>\n+                    {message && <p role='alert'>{message}</p>}\n+                </fieldset>\n                 <AcademyAccount view={snapshot.academy} dispatch={dispatch} />\n+                <DiagnosticsPanel view={snapshot.diagnostics} dispatch={dispatch}>\n+                    <SetupWarningHistory warnings={snapshot.tenants.find((t) => t.id === snapshot.active?.tenant)?.setupWarnings ?? []} />\n+                </DiagnosticsPanel>\n             </div>\n-            <div className='mt-6'>\n-                <TenantsSettings snapshot={snapshot} dispatch={dispatch} observeManagement={observeManagement} />\n-            </div>\n-            <div className='mt-6'>\n-                <DiagnosticsPanel view={snapshot.diagnostics} dispatch={dispatch} />\n-            </div>\n+            <TenantsSettings snapshot={snapshot} dispatch={dispatch} observeManagement={observeManagement} />\n         </section>\n     )\n })\ndiff --git a/apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts b/apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts\nindex b6f136bf..405d567d 100644\n--- a/apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts\n+++ b/apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts\n@@ -94,10 +94,26 @@ export interface Toast {\n  * reload and nothing here is authority: every durable fact is observed from\n  * the Rust snapshot.\n  */\n+/** Unresolved preferred-collection recovery survives page navigation, but never a retired native scope or collection choice. */\n+interface WorkbenchRecovery {\n+    tenant: string | null\n+    context: string | null\n+    collection: string | null\n+    generation: number\n+    pending: boolean\n+    failed: boolean\n+}\n+const initialWorkbenchRecovery = (): WorkbenchRecovery => ({ tenant: null, context: null, collection: null, generation: 0, pending: false, failed: false })\n+\n interface ShellStore {\n     /** The scope the shell shows now (set from each snapshot before it renders): what a notification must belong to. */\n     scope: { tenant: string | null; context: string | null; switchReview: string | null }\n     setScope(tenant: string | null, context: string | null, switchReview?: string | null): void\n+    workbenchRecovery: WorkbenchRecovery\n+    observeWorkbench(tenant: string | null, context: string | null, collection: string | null): void\n+    beginWorkbenchRestore(tenant: string | null, context: string | null): number | null\n+    finishWorkbenchRestore(tenant: string | null, context: string | null, generation: number, failed: boolean): void\n+    resolveWorkbenchRestore(tenant: string | null, context: string | null, generation: number): void\n     paletteOpen: boolean\n     switcherOpen: boolean\n     /** The rail's Administration children shown or hidden (C35; the prototype's `adminNav`). */\n@@ -170,6 +186,29 @@ export const useShellStore = create<ShellStore>((set, get) => ({\n             unconfirmed: s.unconfirmed.filter((u) => unconfirmedInContext(u, context) && (!switchResolution(u.intent) || switchResolution(u.intent)?.review === switchReview)),\n             arrival: s.arrival && s.arrival.tenant !== tenant ? null : s.arrival,\n         })),\n+    workbenchRecovery: initialWorkbenchRecovery(),\n+    observeWorkbench: (tenant, context, collection) => set((s) => {\n+        const old = s.workbenchRecovery\n+        if (old.tenant === tenant && old.context === context && old.collection === collection) return s\n+        return { workbenchRecovery: { tenant, context, collection, generation: old.generation + 1, pending: false, failed: false } }\n+    }),\n+    beginWorkbenchRestore: (tenant, context) => {\n+        const old = get().workbenchRecovery\n+        if (old.tenant !== tenant || old.context !== context || old.collection !== null || old.pending) return null\n+        const generation = old.generation + 1\n+        set({ workbenchRecovery: { ...old, generation, pending: true } })\n+        return generation\n+    },\n+    finishWorkbenchRestore: (tenant, context, generation, failed) => set((s) => {\n+        const old = s.workbenchRecovery\n+        if (old.tenant !== tenant || old.context !== context || old.generation !== generation || !old.pending) return s\n+        return { workbenchRecovery: { ...old, pending: false, failed } }\n+    }),\n+    resolveWorkbenchRestore: (tenant, context, generation) => set((s) => {\n+        const old = s.workbenchRecovery\n+        if (old.tenant !== tenant || old.context !== context || old.generation !== generation) return s\n+        return { workbenchRecovery: { ...old, generation: old.generation + 1, pending: false, failed: false } }\n+    }),\n     paletteOpen: false,\n     switcherOpen: false,\n     adminNavOpen: true,\n@@ -236,5 +275,5 @@ export const useShellStore = create<ShellStore>((set, get) => ({\n \n /** Test seam: forget everything (each test starts from an empty store). */\n export function resetShellStore() {\n-    useShellStore.setState({ scope: { tenant: null, context: null, switchReview: null }, paletteOpen: false, switcherOpen: false, adminNavOpen: true, toasts: [], modals: [], unconfirmed: [], toastMs: 6000, inboxSelection: {}, arrival: null, harnessDrafts: {}, harnessFresh: {}, harnessUnsent: {}, harnessSent: {}, playground: null })\n+    useShellStore.setState({ workbenchRecovery: initialWorkbenchRecovery(), scope: { tenant: null, context: null, switchReview: null }, paletteOpen: false, switcherOpen: false, adminNavOpen: true, toasts: [], modals: [], unconfirmed: [], toastMs: 6000, inboxSelection: {}, arrival: null, harnessDrafts: {}, harnessFresh: {}, harnessUnsent: {}, harnessSent: {}, playground: null })\n }\ndiff --git a/crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs b/crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs\nindex 87348ac6..7aade642 100644\n--- a/crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs\n+++ b/crates/desktop-core/src/features.rs\n@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@ pub struct VerifyView {\n     pub done: bool,\n     /// Some line failed.\n     pub failed: bool,\n-    /// A required line failed (the scan key on first run): completion is\n+    /// The required OAuth authentication failed: completion is\n     /// refused. An optional line's failure is carried as a warning instead.\n     pub blocking: bool,\n     /// The inputs changed since this run started: it no longer counts.\n@@ -138,8 +138,10 @@ pub struct SetupView {\n     /// The draft's profile and credential states (no secret material).\n     pub tenant: crate::TenantView,\n     pub products: Vec<ProductId>,\n-    /// First run requires the scan key; the add sheet does not.\n+    /// Scan keys are configured separately; setup never submits a scan.\n     pub scan_required: bool,\n+    /// Every new tenant requires authenticated management OAuth.\n+    pub management_required: bool,\n     pub packs: Vec<PackView>,\n     /// The Gateway workspace chosen for the draft, with the reference its\n     /// inference key is configured under.\n@@ -162,6 +164,46 @@ pub struct SetupWarning {\n     /// Wall-clock seconds since the Unix epoch when it was recorded\n     /// (`u32`: a JSON number, never a bigint, on the TypeScript side).\n     pub recorded_secs: u32,\n+    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    #[ts(optional)]\n+    pub check: Option<SetupWarningBinding>,\n+    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    #[ts(optional)]\n+    pub recheck: Option<SetupWarningRecheck>,\n+    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n+    #[ts(optional)]\n+    pub resolved_secs: Option<u32>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Scope of the original setup check; absent on historical warnings.\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n+pub struct SetupWarningBinding {\n+    pub version: u8,\n+    pub line: VerifyLine,\n+    pub tsg_id: String,\n+    pub origin: String,\n+    pub workspace: Option<SetupWarningWorkspace>,\n+}\n+\n+/// Gateway IAM uses the listed workspace slug, not its displayed UUID.\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n+pub struct SetupWarningWorkspace {\n+    pub id: String,\n+    pub slug: String,\n+    pub scope_name: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Latest dedicated setup recheck. Original reason/time remain unchanged.\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n+pub struct SetupWarningRecheck {\n+    pub checked_secs: u32,\n+    pub state: VerifyState,\n+    pub reason: String,\n+    pub equivalent: bool,\n+    pub basis: SetupWarningBasis,\n }\n \n /// A Runtime API key named by its identifier and name (never a secret).\n@@ -314,3 +356,13 @@ pub fn default_feature() -> FeatureId {\n         .map(|e| e.id)\n         .unwrap_or(FeatureId::Home)\n }\n+\n+/// How the latest check was related to the original diagnostic.\n+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n+pub enum SetupWarningBasis {\n+    RecordedScope,\n+    LegacyTenantSources,\n+    LegacyWorkspaceScope,\n+    Unknown,\n+}\ndiff --git a/crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs b/crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs\nindex 88622a96..586a38fb 100644\n--- a/crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs\n+++ b/crates/desktop-core/src/store.rs\n@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n \n use crate::tenants::{TenantId, TenantProfile};\n use crate::vault::RecordId;\n-use crate::wire::Theme;\n+use crate::wire::{ColorTheme, Theme};\n \n /// Schema of the persisted state document.\n pub const STATE_SCHEMA: &str = \"prisma-airs-desktop/state/1\";\n@@ -162,6 +162,9 @@ pub struct StoredMcpGrant {\n pub struct PersistedState {\n     pub schema: String,\n     pub appearance: Theme,\n+    /// Missing in earlier state: use the Prisma AIRS family while retaining appearance.\n+    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"ColorTheme::is_default\")]\n+    pub color_theme: ColorTheme,\n     pub tenants: Vec<TenantProfile>,\n     pub active_tenant: Option<TenantId>,\n     pub credentials: Vec<StoredCredential>,\n@@ -256,6 +259,7 @@ impl Default for PersistedState {\n         Self {\n             schema: STATE_SCHEMA.to_owned(),\n             appearance: Theme::System,\n+            color_theme: ColorTheme::default(),\n             tenants: Vec::new(),\n             active_tenant: None,\n             credentials: Vec::new(),\n@@ -719,6 +723,29 @@ mod tests {\n         }\n     }\n \n+    #[test]\n+    fn color_theme_defaults_existing_state_without_changing_appearance() {\n+        let mut value = serde_json::to_value(sample()).expect(\"state\");\n+        assert!(value.get(\"colorTheme\").is_none(), \"default stays omitted\");\n+        let state: PersistedState = serde_json::from_value(value.clone()).expect(\"old state\");\n+        assert_eq!(state.color_theme, ColorTheme::PrismaAirs);\n+        assert_eq!(state.appearance, Theme::Dark);\n+        value[\"colorTheme\"] = serde_json::json!(\"not-a-theme\");\n+        assert!(serde_json::from_value::<PersistedState>(value).is_err());\n+    }\n+\n+    #[test]\n+    fn alternate_color_theme_roundtrips_independently_of_appearance() {\n+        let mut state = sample();\n+        state.color_theme = ColorTheme::Gruvbox;\n+        let value = serde_json::to_value(&state).expect(\"state\");\n+        assert_eq!(value[\"colorTheme\"], \"gruvbox\");\n+        assert_eq!(\n+            serde_json::from_value::<PersistedState>(value).expect(\"new state\"),\n+            state\n+        );\n+    }\n+\n     #[test]\n     fn saves_atomically_with_owner_only_modes_and_reloads() {\n         use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;\ndiff --git a/crates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs b/crates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs\nindex acf63b23..b1c1516d 100644\n--- a/crates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs\n+++ b/crates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs\n@@ -31,6 +31,21 @@ pub enum Theme {\n     Dark,\n }\n \n+/// Desktop palette family, independent of light/dark appearance and Academy.\n+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize, TS)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n+pub enum ColorTheme {\n+    #[default]\n+    PrismaAirs,\n+    Gruvbox,\n+}\n+\n+impl ColorTheme {\n+    pub fn is_default(&self) -> bool {\n+        *self == Self::PrismaAirs\n+    }\n+}\n+\n /// One Intent delivery from the renderer.\n #[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Deserialize, TS)]\n #[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\", deny_unknown_fields)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
