{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/architecture/desktop-themes.md; rg -n 'color_theme|ColorTheme|EditTenant|edit_tenant|DeleteTenant|delete_tenant' crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs crates/desktop-core/src/context.rs crates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs; cat crates/desktop-core/tests/refinement_metadata.rs\"","aggregated_output":"# Desktop color themes\n\nThe desktop owns two independent preferences: appearance (`system`, `light`,\n`dark`) and color theme (`prismaAirs`, `gruvbox`). Prisma AIRS is the default.\nNeither preference updates an Academy account or unlocks an earned cosmetic.\n\nExisting state without `colorTheme` defaults to Prisma AIRS and retains its\nappearance. The default is omitted when saving; an alternate theme is saved as\nan explicit field. Invalid theme values remain a storage error, rather than\nsilently overwriting the preference. Existing atomic storage writes apply.\n\nOlder binaries use strict field validation and can reject state written with a\nnew preference. Opening an upgraded data directory with an older release is\nunsupported; this change does not claim downgrade compatibility or silently\nreset data. Preserve the state before any explicitly requested downgrade.\n\nThe document's general Academy theme continues to follow appearance. Desktop\npalette tokens are independent, and shared presentation colors are adapted only\ninside desktop theme scopes. Academy content and its portals keep the general\nAcademy palette. Earned Academy themes remain under Academy's existing rules.\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:37:pub enum ColorTheme {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:43:impl ColorTheme {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:93:use crate::wire::{ColorTheme, Theme};\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:121:    SetColorTheme {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:122:        theme: ColorTheme,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:233:    EditTenant {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:238:    DeleteTenant {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:770:    SetColorTheme => \"setColorTheme\",\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:790:    EditTenant => \"editTenant\",\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:791:    DeleteTenant => \"deleteTenant\",\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1181:    pub color_theme: ColorTheme,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1621:    color_theme: ColorTheme,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1819:    fn color_theme(&self) -> ColorTheme {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1820:        self.data.color_theme\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1861:            color_theme: self.color_theme(),\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1953:            color_theme: self.color_theme(),\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3316:        color_theme: doc.color_theme,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3573:        Intent::SetColorTheme { theme } => {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3574:            if state.color_theme() != theme {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3576:                state.data.color_theme = theme;\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3891:        Intent::EditTenant {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3920:        Intent::DeleteTenant { tenant } => {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:6096:    async fn color_theme_is_persisted_without_changing_appearance_or_tenant_scope() {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:6113:                Intent::SetColorTheme {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:6114:                    theme: ColorTheme::Gruvbox,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:6121:        assert_eq!(after.color_theme, ColorTheme::Gruvbox);\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:6125:        assert_eq!(saved.color_theme, ColorTheme::Gruvbox);\n#![cfg(feature = \"test-fixtures\")]\n\nuse desktop_core::features::TenantEnvironment;\nuse desktop_core::fixtures::{self, ScriptedStore};\nuse desktop_core::store::PersistedState;\nuse desktop_core::tenants::{Destination, Region, TenantId, TenantProfile};\nuse desktop_core::{\n    Core, CoreConfig, Delivery, Intent, Observation, Refusal, ShellSnapshot, ViewScope,\n};\nuse serde_json::json;\n\nfn profile(id: &str, label: &str) -> TenantProfile {\n    TenantProfile {\n        id: TenantId::parse(id).expect(\"fixture id\"),\n        label: label.to_owned(),\n        tsg_id: Some(\"1234567890\".to_owned()),\n        destination: Destination::Region {\n            region: Region::Europe,\n        },\n        environment: TenantEnvironment::Production,\n    }\n}\nfn snapshot(core: &Core) -> ShellSnapshot {\n    match core.operator().observe(ViewScope::Shell).expect(\"snapshot\") {\n        Observation::Shell { snapshot, .. } => snapshot,\n        _ => panic!(\"shell expected\"),\n    }\n}\nfn state() -> PersistedState {\n    let a = profile(\"tn-0123456789abcdef\", \"A\");\n    let b = profile(\"tn-fedcba9876543210\", \"B\");\n    PersistedState {\n        tenants: vec![a.clone(), b],\n        active_tenant: Some(a.id),\n        ..PersistedState::default()\n    }\n}\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn metadata_edit_targets_only_the_selected_profile_without_rebinding_identity() {\n    let (adapters, handles) = fixtures::adapters_with(ScriptedStore::with_state(state()));\n    let core = Core::new(\n        CoreConfig {\n            fixture_tenant_creation: false,\n            ..CoreConfig::default()\n        },\n        adapters,\n    );\n    core.start();\n    let before = snapshot(&core);\n    let handle = core.operator();\n    let session = handle.register_delivery_session().expect(\"session\").nonce;\n    let target = before.tenants[1].id.clone();\n    handle\n        .dispatch(\n            Delivery {\n                session,\n                sequence: 1,\n            },\n            Intent::EditTenant {\n                tenant: target.clone(),\n                label: \"Renamed B\".to_owned(),\n                environment: TenantEnvironment::Staging,\n            },\n        )\n        .await\n        .expect(\"metadata edit\");\n    let after = snapshot(&core);\n    assert_eq!(\n        after.active, before.active,\n        \"metadata never switches the active tenant\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(after.tenants[0], before.tenants[0]);\n    let changed = &after.tenants[1];\n    assert_eq!(changed.id, target);\n    assert_eq!(changed.label, \"Renamed B\");\n    assert_eq!(changed.environment, TenantEnvironment::Staging);\n    assert_eq!(changed.tsg_id, before.tenants[1].tsg_id);\n    assert_eq!(changed.destination, before.tenants[1].destination);\n    assert_eq!(changed.management, before.tenants[1].management);\n    assert_eq!(changed.scan, before.tenants[1].scan);\n    assert_eq!(\n        handles.store.saved().expect(\"saved\").tenants[1].label,\n        \"Renamed B\"\n    );\n}\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn metadata_edit_rolls_back_when_private_persistence_fails() {\n    let (adapters, handles) = fixtures::adapters_with(ScriptedStore::with_state(state()));\n    let core = Core::new(\n        CoreConfig {\n            fixture_tenant_creation: false,\n            ..CoreConfig::default()\n        },\n        adapters,\n    );\n    core.start();\n    let before = snapshot(&core);\n    handles.store.fail_saves(true);\n    let handle = core.operator();\n    let session = handle.register_delivery_session().expect(\"session\").nonce;\n    assert!(\n        handle\n            .dispatch(\n                Delivery {\n                    session,\n                    sequence: 1\n                },\n                Intent::EditTenant {\n                    tenant: before.tenants[0].id.clone(),\n                    label: \"Not saved\".to_owned(),\n                    environment: TenantEnvironment::Other,\n                }\n            )\n            .await\n            .is_err()\n    );\n    let after = snapshot(&core);\n    assert_eq!(after.tenants, before.tenants);\n    assert_eq!(after.active, before.active);\n    assert_eq!(\n        handles.store.saved().expect(\"old saved state\").tenants[0].label,\n        \"A\"\n    );\n}\n#[tokio::test]\nasync fn metadata_edit_rejects_invalid_labels_and_has_no_tsg_or_endpoint_fields() {\n    let (adapters, _) = fixtures::adapters_with(ScriptedStore::with_state(state()));\n    let core = Core::new(\n        CoreConfig {\n            fixture_tenant_creation: false,\n            ..CoreConfig::default()\n        },\n        adapters,\n    );\n    core.start();\n    let before = snapshot(&core);\n    let handle = core.operator();\n    let session = handle.register_delivery_session().expect(\"session\").nonce;\n    assert_eq!(\n        handle\n            .dispatch(\n                Delivery {\n                    session,\n                    sequence: 1\n                },\n                Intent::EditTenant {\n                    tenant: before.tenants[0].id.clone(),\n                    label: \"   \".to_owned(),\n                    environment: TenantEnvironment::Other,\n                }\n            )\n            .await,\n        Err(Refusal::InvalidInput)\n    );\n    for (field, value) in [\n        (\"tsgId\", json!(\"9999999999\")),\n        (\"destination\", json!({\"kind\":\"region\", \"region\":\"india\"})),\n    ] {\n        let mut intent = json!({\"kind\":\"editTenant\", \"tenant\":before.tenants[0].id, \"label\":\"A\", \"environment\":\"production\"});\n        intent[field] = value;\n        assert!(\n            serde_json::from_value::<Intent>(intent).is_err(),\n            \"unreviewed identity field {field}\"\n        );\n    }\n    assert_eq!(snapshot(&core).tenants, before.tenants);\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
